{"text": "Entonces lo que habla Mosé Yair en el Likutei Moharan, de \"Lismjoh geulah litfilah\". Entonces todo es \"Lismjoh geulah litfilah\". Basically, geulah es la emuná. Yotam dice, es-- no empieza de ti, empieza de Hashem. Si tú te vas al lugar donde realmente empieza Hashem, en ese lugar tú te quedas callado. No vamos a decir más. Primero, hay tira entre geulah y tefilah. De la misma manera que hay tira entre emuná y tefilah. ¿Por qué? Si acá se enfocara la... Pues para qué pides tefilah. Entonces, Hashem hace todo.", "language_code": "spa", "language_probability": 1, "words": [{"text": "Entonces", "start": 0, "end": 0.4, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 0.4, "end": 0.42, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "lo", "start": 0.42, "end": 0.5, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 0.5, "end": 0.54, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "que", "start": 0.54, "end": 0.58, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.6, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "habla", "start": 0.6, "end": 0.78, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 0.78, "end": 0.82, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "Mosé", "start": 0.82, "end": 1, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 1, "end": 1.06, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "Yair", "start": 1.06, "end": 1.34, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 1.34, "end": 1.44, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "en", "start": 1.44, "end": 1.56, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 1.56, "end": 1.62, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "el", "start": 1.62, "end": 1.94, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 1.94, "end": 2.24, "type": "spacing", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": "Likutei", "start": 2.24, "end": 2.6, "type": "word", "speaker_id": null}, {"text": " ", "start": 2.6, "e